Web-only, applied by build-web.sh after web-record-cap.patch and reverted after the build.
react-native-web fires onPress only from a DOM click. A press whose target is swapped mid-press (stop
square -> Continue disc) or a long touch hold gets no click, so the flag left by that press ate the next
tap and the first Continue did nothing. Each press now starts with clean flags, a quick tap no longer
opens two MediaRecorders, and a held touch on Android is no longer cut off by contextmenu (~0.45 s).

